# Keeping the STATUS tab true.
#
# A science tab is a stored string: the scan writes it once and re-selecting the
# contact never runs that block again. So something has to push. The ticker does the
# ordinary work (a shield coming back, a countdown falling), and the dirty signal is
# for the moments worth landing in the same frame - an elite committing to an ability,
# or being talked out of it.
#
# Both are //shared/signal, not //signal. The write is indexed by the SCANNING SIDE,
# so one console doing it is the whole side done; five consoles each starting a watcher
# is five tickers writing the same blob. SIGNAL_ROUTING.md.

//shared/signal/game_started
    task_schedule(science_status_watch)

//shared/signal/science_status_dirty
    science_status_push(STATUS_ID)


=== science_status_watch
" Re-render every contact a science officer has scanned. Only lines that actually
" moved are written, and the registry only holds ships somebody scanned, so this is a
" walk over a handful of ids rather than over the world.
--- science_status_beat
    await delay_sim(1)
    science_status_tick()
    jump science_status_beat
